# One line-ending truth across every machine and clone: every text file is
# LF in the repository AND in the working tree. Editors and tools reading
# this (VS Code, git-bash, PowerShell, python, node) all read and write LF
# fine, and a mixed-EOL working tree is what happens otherwise — a Windows
# checkout can render CRLF (Git-for-Windows' system core.autocrlf=true)
# while LF-preferring tools insert their own lines into it, producing
# `w/mixed` files. Binary formats
# are pinned explicitly so auto-detection never has to decide; eol=lf
# beats any local core.autocrlf config.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png -text
*.webp -text
*.jpg -text
*.wav -text
